Bayesian population inference supplies a prescription for evaluating the likelihood of our set \\mathbf{d} of GW observations, given a population model \\pi(m_{1},m_{2}|\\mathbf{\\lambda}) that depends on unknown population parameters \\mathbf{\\lambda}(Mandel, 2010; Mandel et al., 2019). Formally,

